    "encoding_note": "PSI5 data is Manchester-coded onto current pulses (nominal +-26 mA) on a two-wire current loop. There is no separate clock wire — the Manchester mid-bit transitions embed the bit clock. The telegram is protected by a 2-bit/3-bit CRC or parity. Bit rates are 125 and 189 kbps."
